This repository uses different licenses for content and code. These are not
alternative licenses for the same material.

1. Original documentation and curation

Unless an individual item states otherwise, original protocol descriptions,
explanatory documentation, authored figures, and original curation annotations
are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
(SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0).
Full license: LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

2. Original software

Unless an individual file states otherwise, original software in scripts/,
original Python tools in analysis/diann/, original executable JavaScript and styling in assets/, original SVG artwork,
and build configuration (_quarto.yml and .github/workflows/) are licensed under
the MIT License (SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT).
Full license: LICENSES/MIT.txt

3. Datasets and third-party material

The content license covers only rights held by the author in original material.
It does not relicense third-party papers, manuals, figures, software, databases,
dataset contents, trademarks, or institutional logos. Their original terms apply.
External links and citations do not transfer ownership or grant additional rights.

Each future dataset must identify its own license, provenance, and redistribution
conditions. A dataset without an explicit license is not automatically licensed
under CC BY 4.0 or MIT by its appearance in this repository. Authored descriptions
of datasets and the underlying datasets must be considered separately.

Author affiliation identifies the maintainer; it does not imply institutional
ownership, sponsorship, approval, or endorsement of this personal resource.

